From: giovannipodesta
Subject: [PATCH] xnu: 0335 — comments only: state what the code and the measurements say

Comment-only. Rewrites comments that state facts contradicted by dev-notes/investigacion
(01 audit, 03 measurements, 06): sweet_usb (boot-path state of the DWC3, delay() blocking,
late-not-lost events, 0327/ud_watch reclaim, 0328 target, defaults of sweetusb_dp and
sweetusb_utmipipe), sweet_reboot / SweetPlatformExpert (restart modes and how iOS boots),
sweet_ufs (ufsroot=iosroot on dual boot, which slot kern.sweet_boot_android activates),
caches.c (flush_dcache/clean_dcache are real on this board) and SWEET.h (topaz is ARMv8.0).
The comment-stripped token stream of every file is identical before and after.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_reboot.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_reboot.c
index 0628506..fffc033 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_reboot.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_reboot.c
@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@
 /*
  * sapphire 0221: where a restart goes (SweetPlatformExpert::haltRestart). sysctl
- * kern.sweet_reboot_mode = 0 system (Android, from the boot partition), 1 recovery, 2 bootloader
- * (fastboot, the default: iOS is only ever started with fastboot boot); boot-arg sweet_reboot=N
- * sets the default.
+ * kern.sweet_reboot_mode = 0 system: a normal boot of the GPT's active slot (boot_<slot>), which is
+ * iOS itself when iOS's slot is active (the installed layout flashes iOS into boot_<iOS slot>) and
+ * Android only after kern.sweet_boot_android switched slots; 1 recovery; 2 bootloader (fastboot),
+ * the default. Boot-arg sweet_reboot=N sets the default.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
